1a:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-amber-200 text-gray-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Your task: "}],"Know how to find your actual scope, and what to do when a request falls outside it."]}]
1b:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Scope of practice is the set of tasks a person may legally perform. For licensed roles it is defined by a practice act. Medical assistants are unlicensed in most states, so their scope derives from what a supervising provider may lawfully delegate — and that varies substantially from one state to the next."}]
1c:["$","p","2",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"This is genuinely different from most professions, and it is the single most important thing to understand about the role. A task you performed daily in one state may be prohibited in another. Your competence is not the question; the delegating authority is."}]
